# LF everywhere. The hooks and validators are POSIX shell and .mjs, and several of
# their parsers end row regexes with `$` and no `m` flag — a CRLF checkout parses the
# constraints registry to zero rows while every gate still reports green. That exact
# defect shipped once and was caught only by testing a CRLF file directly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shipped as executables; a CRLF shebang dies with `env: sh\r: No such file or directory`.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
